changes.change:
Align the fold row on its first line instead of its center. When the line does not fit beside the title, it wraps whole onto the next flex line (open too) instead of into a narrow column beside the title. Proven in C:\Users\stephen\AppData\Local\Temp\hw-tfa-ux\proto-UX\com.lawrensen.hwinfo.sdPlugin\ui\proto-R.css (tail block):

details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name { flex-wrap: wrap; }
details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name > .hw-label { line-height: 24px; }
@media (max-width: 299px) {
  details.hw-look-fold:not([open]) > summary.hw-look-name .hw-look-current { flex: 0 1 auto; }
  details.hw-look-fold[open] > summary.hw-look-name > .hw-label { line-height: inherit; }
  details.hw-look-fold[open] > summary.hw-look-name::before { top: 7px; }
}

changes.why:
MEASURED (out2/R/lab2.json, sheet-align.png): R centers the title on the whole wrapped block, so it leaves its marker's line:
- 13.2 px ("neon-2031") and 21.6 px ("synthwave-sunset-2027") folded at 189 and 160, where the title floats mid-block beside a three-line column and the marker sits alone at the top;
- 4.8 px folded on a dial at 249, with "(set on this / dial)" in two lines beside the chip;
- 4.8 px open at 373 and 320 with a long unknown id;
- 2.9 px open at 189 and 160 in every state.
Every other section keeps its title on the marker's line and wraps its summary under it, so these rows stop reading as a section in exactly the states the brief's question 5 names (unknown stored theme, 200% zoom).

MEASURED in the trial:
- Marker to title is at most 0.1 px in all 60 cases.
- Known-theme rows keep R's exact heights, and chip tops per width are identical to R's.
- Costs fall only on rare states: an unknown id wraps under the title (open 48.8 px at 373 instead of 39.6); a dial at 249 folds to 47.8 instead of 40.6.

